Expected elements: present

All four changes landed. (1) The provenance note is its own grid-spanning `dd`, flush left at x=1541 under the `DATA` row (y 210–380). (2) `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` reads `1755555891986239551` in base ten at #242424, ending x≈1903 with an 11px gutter to the pane rule at x=1915 — my last-round finding is resolved, and the label/value grid is intact. (3) The decoded-input note renders its no-call-data variant (y 742–828). (4) The exit reads `← aztec-testnet`; no synthetic slug, no fixture content, no invented file, line or symbol names. The `⊙`/`⊘` glyphs do not appear — this trace has no source, so there is no current-line band and the prior 2.40:1 measurement cannot be retaken here.

Text contrast is genuinely good: labels #565656/white 7.34:1, prose #484848 9.15:1, values #242424 15.5:1, links #4F46E5 6.29:1, badges 6.49:1 and 6.61:1. One exception below.

The palette, though, is inherited rather than designed: every accent is a literal framework default across four unrelated hue families, and the badge system spends two tones on six meanings.

Top fixes: give provenance and the `Pending`/absence states tones of their own, and put the `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` block in the editor palette.

Rating: 6/10

